api.yaml; do not add extra role rules.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-2\",\n  \"question\": \"What should happen for paths or HTTP methods that are not defined in the contract?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Use normal 404/405 responses and add no undocumented operations.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-3\",\n  \"question\": \"If demo seed data cannot be written to PostgreSQL when Seed:Demo is true, how should startup behave?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Fail startup and surface the seed-write error.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-4\",\n  \"question\": \"Should successful API writes remain available after the API process restarts?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Use normal PostgreSQL durability so successful writes remain available after an API restart.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"sentences\" kind=\"restated\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"n\": 1,\n  \"text\": \"Implement the Feedlot API exactly as declared in contracts/openapi.yaml, with no undocumented operations or product-screen routes, and return contract-defined authentication, session, dashboard, and filtered lot data.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 2,\n  \"text\": \"Implement procurement imports and allocations with contract-defined matching, PO-line-to-lot and lot-to-pen traceability, saved quantities, capacity information, and conflict results.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 3,\n  \"text\": \"Implement lot forecasts, forecast-setting updates, metrics, insights, planner actions, and weight-history operations with contract-defined values, calculations, suggestions, validation, and persisted updates.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 4,\n  \"text\": \"Implement inventory reads, writes, movements, projections, and CSV exports with contract-defined stock values and persist valid inventory changes in PostgreSQL.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 5,\n  \"text\": \"Implement ration reads, creation, revision, optimization, and approval with contract-defined data, calculations, results, and persisted changes.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 6,\n  \"text\": \"Implement feed-plan reads, creation, review, and status changes with contract-defined pen-level details, calculated quantities, audit state, and persisted status.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 7,\n  \"text\": \"Implement feeding-event reads, creation, correction, and voiding with contract-defined variance, cost, energy, inventory movements, and updated lot feed totals, and persist the events and related changes.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 8,\n  \"text\": \"Implement operational, feed-to-gain, and profitability reports and exports with contract-defined filters, permission-filtered rows, calculations, summaries, and artifacts.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 9,\n  \"text\": \"Implement sample-data status, loading, reset, and replacement operations with contract-defined records and statuses, avoid duplicate loading, and require explicit confirmation for reset or replacement.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 10,\n  \"text\": \"Store contract domain data in the PostgreSQL database configured by the App connection string, preserve successful writes across API restarts, and upgrade the domain schema without changing existing data.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 11,\n  \"text\": \"When Seed:Demo is true, run SeedData.Run at startup to add 3 to 5 believable, contract-example-derived sample rows to each empty application table, leave nonempty tables unchanged, and fail startup while surfacing any seed-write error.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 12,\n  \"text\": \"When Seed:Demo is false, serve collection operations from persisted records only, including empty collections when no records exist.\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\nMap the sentences."}